[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186184219,
      "id": "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2",
      "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6c6a1ecf-5a27-5fb9-aff9-9ea89e393b50",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $10\\times 12$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=7,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+7 & =12 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =12-7 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "92dc3489-2d57-5de3-9e94-b1c0c02d432c",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
