      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $12\\times 11$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=11.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =11 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =11-3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
